id           = CWE-79
name         = Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')
abstraction  = Base
structure    = Simple
status       = Stable

description : The product does not neutralize or incorrectly neutralizes user-controllable input before it is placed in output that is used as a web page that is served to other users.

extended description : There are many variants of cross-site scripting, characterized by a variety of terms or involving different attack topologies. However, they all indicate the same fundamental weakness: improper neutralization of dangerous input between the adversary and a victim.

notes : https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html
